What the records say (agents/seam_fp/out_f5_*.txt, out_f5_tail_check.txt), campaign 34, requests to minute 110:
- 63 to 75 % of SSD lookups found nothing (4,883 to 5,759 of 7,451 to 8,110 an arm); on TraceLab (campaign 33
  ec_full) 3,686 of 3,710.
- 3,981 and 4,293 planned turns (ec_full, jit_exact) had an arrival lookup that found nothing; for 91.5 to 91.9 %
  of them chain - matched equals the previous reply's length to within one page, and for 0.6 to 0.8 % history was
  really missing from memory. Way B removes these lookups.
- At an empty queue such a turn waited a median 17.7 ms for admission against 1.1 to 1.4 ms for a turn the gate
  called covered (campaign 33: 15.5 against 0.9 ms, on 2,469 of 6,778 requests).
- Turns admitted without their history after the gate answered capped: 3 (ec_full), 10 (jit_exact), 26 (jit_p50),
  1 (ec_exact), carrying 4.6, 19.8, 51.7 and 2.1 % of the history each arm computed again (0.06, 0.30, 0.85 and
  0.02 M tokens); in all but 3 of jit_p50's 26 every lookup the turn had made found nothing. Campaign 32 ec_full:
  133 turns, 4.2 M tokens, 20 %.
